message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
type: software

title: "Adaptive VICReg in TensorFlow/Keras"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2025-11-24"

authors:
  - family-names: Kabra
    given-names: Nishant
    affiliation: "Illinois Institute of Technology"

repository-code: "https://github.com/nkabra56/adaptive-vicreg"
license-url: "https://github.com/nkabra56/adaptive-vicreg/blob/main/LICENSE"
keywords:
  - self-supervised learning
  - VICReg
  - adaptive loss weighting
  - TensorFlow
  - CIFAR-10

abstract: >
  A TensorFlow/Keras implementation of VICReg (Variance-Invariance-Covariance
  Regularization) with an experimental adaptive variant that reweights the three
  loss terms during self-supervised pretraining on CIFAR-10. Includes scripts for
  pretraining, linear and kNN evaluation, and plotting.
